        "about": "<p>Udhayanidhi Stalin (born 27 November 1977) is an Indian politician and the incumbent Opposition Leader of Tamil Nadu Legislative Assembly since May 2026. He also served as the third Deputy Chief minister of Tamil Nadu from 2024 to 2026. Udhayanidhi is the son of M. K. Stalin, the eighth Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu. He is the third and the youngest to hold the position of deputy chief minister of the state. Udhayanidhi has served as the minister of youth welfare and sports development since December 2022.</p><p>Udhayanidhi attended the Don Bosco Matriculation Higher Secondary School in Egmore, Madras and later received a degree in commerce from Loyola College, Chennai. Prior to his career as a politician, he was an actor who also produced and distributed films through his Red Giant Movies.</p><p>In 2019, Udhayanidhi entered into politics after being appointed as the secretary of the youth wing of the Dravida Munnetra Kazhagam, led by his father Stalin. In 2021, he was elected as a Member of the Tamil Nadu Legislative Assembly from the Chepauk-Thiruvallikeni Assembly constituency.</p>",
